1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset
floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off.

3
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:33,020
Maybe I'll get to save up for it, I wonder,

4
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed at me for still being a kid.

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow lose my energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
pachinko, a sigh, a yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
the streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the water bottle of the pointed hat,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset sinks into the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this, won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,020
In Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness has been lost.

12
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:25,060
Because I've been drenched in tears.

13
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:31,560
Matsutake Security Squad, move out!

14
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:35,300
Pantakey!

15
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:42,680
Delicious, truly paradise on earth!

16
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,720
All together: Yay!

17
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:47,620
Lower your head!

18
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:48,920
Kneel before me!

19
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:50,560
*pant* *pant*

20
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:56,760
Behold! Top-grade Kyoto matsutake,
100,000 yen per kilo!

21
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,620
Quite the aroma, isn't it?

22
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:07,040
Really... so this is the scent of matsutake?

23
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:13,980
It's imported from Canada,
but at 8,000 yen a kilo, it's a bargain.

24
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,560
When it comes to the king of autumn delicacies,
it's matsutake.

25
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:23,880
Eating seasonal produce first
is what makes a true Edokko!

26
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:27,800
You lot should be grateful
just to get to see them.

27
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:31,860
Now we'll cook matsutake that
costs 100,000 yen per kilo.

28
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:35,040
I saw them lined up at the
greengrocer's on the way here.

29
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:39,020
I splurged so we could
all enjoy grilled matsutake.

30
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:42,200
I hear there are imports
from Europe these days too.

31
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:46,920
Even us common folk can
now enjoy matsutake casually.

32
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:49,940
Ideally,
we'd grill them over bincho charcoal, but...

33
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:53,280
Since it's an import anyway, gas will do.

34
00:02:56,440 --> 00:03:00,980
Now, we'll grill the 100,000-yen-per-kilo
matsutake over bincho charcoal.

35
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:04,640
As a slightly belated
summer gift for everyone,

36
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:08,160
we're offering you the
aroma of matsutake for free.

37
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:14,460
Shut up! Be grateful for the aroma alone!

38
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,540
Wow, what a great smell!

39
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:19,660
Gotta be careful not to burn them.

40
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:20,560
Yes.

41
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:27,900
Wow, delicious, precious, ambitious!

42
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,138
But,

43
00:03:29,188 --> 00:03:33,260
it's a shame to eat such a
fine mushroom all by myself.

44
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:38,460
That's it, let's show off to
those guys from the department.

45
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:40,740
Alright, here we go!

46
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:45,080
Just give me a little bit,
that's all I'm asking.

47
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,720
Move it, move it!

48
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:52,420
I'm going to eat these piping hot matsutake right in front of the Chief and the others,
rubbing it in!

49
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,020
Here they come, here they come!

50
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:56,360
Chief...

51
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,660
May I take a little home with me?

52
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:04,060
I'd feel bad eating it all alone,
with my family at home.

53
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:08,220
Of course, of course!

54
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:10,520
You're a family man, Terai.

55
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,180
Really.

56
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,900
Well then, shall we dig in?

57
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:21,380
Thank you for the food!

58
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:23,960
Hey, it's matsutake!

59
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:49,200
Wow, so many matsutake!

60
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:50,360
Don't mix them up!

61
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:52,820
What is it, Ryotsu?

62
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:55,060
You brought matsutake too?

63
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,020
They've gotten mixed up,
and now I can't tell them apart.

64
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:03,140
Chief Ohara too, for us,

65
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:05,620
bought matsutake from Kaneda-san.

66
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,140
K-Kaneda-san?

67
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:11,440
Come on, Ryo-chan.
Let's eat them while they're hot.

68
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:12,320
Wait!

69
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,920
What's wrong, senpai?

70
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:17,700
Don't be ridiculous. Don't lump these
in with the Chief's cheap imports!

71
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:18,620
Stingy?

72
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:20,430
My matsutake,

73
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:23,560
is top-quality domestic stuff
that costs 100,000 yen a kilo!

74
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,100
100,000 a kilo?

75
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:28,440
That's right.
It's not something poor people eat.

76
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:32,500
Then, Ryo-chan, why don't you just pick out
the matsutake you bought yourself and eat those?

77
00:05:33,380 --> 00:05:36,580
Eat those? How are we supposed to know
which one's the 100,000 yen matsutake?

78
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:39,760
They may look similar,
but the aroma is completely different.

79
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:43,020
Since you went out of your way
to buy the expensive matsutake,

80
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:45,440
there must be a taste that's
worth the price, right?

81
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,000
Hey, Ryotsu.

82
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:51,440
If you don't eat them soon,
they'll get cold.

83
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:52,520
H-hey, Reiko!

84
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,000
This is...

85
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:56,500
Sorry about this, Ryotsu.

86
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,060
S-sorry? What do you mean?

87
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:00,440
Chief, please eat the Canadian ones.

88
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,140
Don't be so stiff about it.

89
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:04,500
You were planning to eat them with everyone too,
weren't you?

90
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,500
...and you went out of your way to bring them,
didn't you?

91
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,080
That's...

92
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:10,080
A good one!

93
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:12,000
Nakagawa, you jerk!

94
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:15,580
As expected, the expensive
matsutake really do smell different.

95
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:18,080
They really are, they're delicious!

96
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:18,900
*Crunch*

97
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:21,380
Hey, you've only taken my matsutake!

98
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:24,000
If you don't eat faster,
there won't be any left for you, senpai.

99
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,200
I know.

100
00:06:26,088 --> 00:06:31,200
Domestic or imported,
I can't tell which is which at all.

101
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:34,700
Okay, this one.

102
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:38,820
Yes! My mouth is in paradise!

103
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,020
Kaneda, yours looks delicious too.

104
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:46,080
Hehe, the imported ones are pretty good too,
aren't they?

105
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,600
Damn it, this time for sure.

106
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:52,280
Wow, this is the real deal.

107
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:54,340
Imports, wait your turn, Pyo-chan.

108
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:58,500
At this point, even a shot from a
bad gun might hit if you fire enough.

109
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:02,660
I can't just sit here and savor it anymore!

110
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:06,020
Ryo-san

111
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:07,720
You're clever with that.

112
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,860
Eating nothing but imported stuff,

113
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:14,840
you don't even know what good food tastes like, yet you go and buy something way beyond your means.
Serves you right.

114
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:20,740
Give it back! Give me back my 100,000 yen!

115
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:26,840
W-what?

116
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:28,120
Hey, wait a sec.

117
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:32,860
Yoshinori-chan, what are you looking at?

118
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:05,400
Ohara's a little petty You're mine.

119
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:08,080
He's been like that for over four hours now.

120
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:09,360
Yeah.

121
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:12,120
Maybe that was a bit cruel.

122
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,940
Come on, just leave him be.

123
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:17,580
Ryo-chan ate plenty of the Chief's matsutake too,
after all.

124
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,040
Yeah, but...

125
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:20,860
There it is, Chief.

126
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:22,360
Ryo-san's miracle cure.

127
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:23,920
Ryo-tsuno?

128
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,320
Matsutake hunting, a perfect autumn outing.

129
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:29,980
I was thinking of going with my family,

130
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:32,700
but I just got a whole bunch of matsutake.

131
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:35,960
Besides, I thought this sort
of thing suits you, Ryo-san.

132
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:37,020
Yeah, that's true.

133
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,340
If it's Senior, he could win back

134
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:42,240
the amount we ate, easily.

135
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,600
If that would put Ryo-chan in a better mood,

136
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,900
it'd be a bargain, don't you think?

137
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:49,300
Yeah, I suppose so.

138
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:52,060
Otherwise he'll hold a
grudge against us for life.

139
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:09,040
It'll take two hours.

140
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:10,920
We're gonna pick and
pick and pick like crazy!

141
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:11,780
Got it?

142
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:13,580
Leave it to me.

143
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,000
Gentlemen, both of you.

144
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,860
Mountain or river,

145
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:18,780
my bike can get us there in one go!

146
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:21,240
Alright, let's go with that plan!

147
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:24,540
He seems to have completely cheered up.

148
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:25,760
That's good, Chief.

149
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:26,400
Yeah.

150
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:29,880
Are you the Ohara party from
the matsutake hunting course?

151
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:34,700
I'm Matsukichi Takeyama,
the landowner around here.

152
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:37,000
Pleased to meet you.

153
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:39,000
Well then, let's get going.

154
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:44,340
Hey, you there!
Past this point, get off the bikes, get off!

155
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:45,620
What?!

156
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:50,340
Understood.

157
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:55,720
What's this guy?
Looks like we got a weird customer.

158
00:09:57,300 --> 00:10:02,100
Hey, old man, what's this matsutake
mountain season rights thing?

159
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:07,820
That's something I started separately from the mushroom hunting,
intending to lease out the land.

160
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:13,500
Matsui, there were no customers at all,
so I ended up with that leftover land.

161
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:16,780
Let's just dump it on these guys.

162
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:21,700
You've got a keen eye, sir.

163
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:29,080
The three hectares roped off are
the best land we've got this time.

164
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:30,960
Wow, that's huge.

165
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:37,320
Right now, the rights to this red pine forest where
you can pick loads of matsutake are just 150,000 yen.

166
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:42,500
Unlike regular mushroom hunting, you can come pick
them anytime during the season, so it's a great deal.

167
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:46,200
So if we pick more than 150,000 yen worth of matsutake,
we'll make a profit?

168
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:50,360
But looking at it, I don't see any
sign of the matsutake that matters most.

169
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:52,520
N-no, that's not true at all!

170
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,586
Last year, for example,

171
00:10:53,636 --> 00:10:58,100
the next mountain over had a huge matsutake harvest,
and it even made the newspaper.

172
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:01,020
They say it brought in nearly 1 million yen.

173
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:02,140
1 million!?

174
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:06,980
Is that story true!?

175
00:11:06,980 --> 00:11:09,080
Will it really be worth 1 million!?

176
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:11,508
W-well, it depends on the district and city,

177
00:11:11,558 --> 00:11:14,620
but even at the very least,
you get back double what you paid.

178
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:19,120
Chief, let's drop the matsutake
hunt and do this instead.

179
00:11:19,540 --> 00:11:23,460
But spending 150,000 yen
would be a major budget overrun.

180
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:25,780
You heard what he said, Chief.

181
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:30,120
The 150,000 yen you pay will
come back as at least 300,000.

182
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:33,240
I dislike that kind of gambling.

183
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:37,540
It's a chance to make money,
and you're being so stubborn, Chief!

184
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:38,720
Fine.

185
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:43,360
By the way, Chief,
how is your grandson Daisuke doing?

186
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:46,780
Daisuke will be so happy.

187
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:50,640
If only he could run through
the mountains with his grandpa.

188
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:51,940
I-I see.

189
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,480
This is the contract.

190
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,740
Just a signature and the deposit,
and that's all, okay?

191
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:16,260
If you don't mind,
we'd like to think it over a little longer.

192
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:18,800
You're still saying that, Chief?

193
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,640
Shut up, idiot.

194
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:22,840
What do you mean, idiot? Idiot, really?

195
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:27,220
Senpai, don't you think 150,000 yen
is too cheap for an area this size?

196
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:30,620
Whether there are any matsutake
here is pretty doubtful.

197
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:34,500
Then if there's more than 150,000 yen's worth of matsutake,
that's fine, right?

198
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:37,820
The base of the red pine is where the matsutake come up,
you know.

199
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:38,500
Alright!

200
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,540
Hey, Ryotsu, what are you doing?

201
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:47,800
Isn't it obvious?
I'm using my sense of smell, sense of smell.

202
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,920
Senpai, aren't you supposed to be a dog?

203
00:12:57,980 --> 00:12:58,780
Found it!

204
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:01,380
Just like Ryotsu.

205
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:03,480
You've got a good nose, you know.

206
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:07,240
Chief, I'll find you 150,000
yen's worth right away.

207
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:10,740
We weren't limited to
imported or domestic, though.

208
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:13,740
Can you actually smell the matsutake itself?

209
00:13:13,740 --> 00:13:18,720
Senpai shows superhuman abilities
whenever money is involved.

210
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,380
Alright, at this rate,
we'll find matsutake one after another...

211
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:28,900
N-no way.

212
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:32,060
Well then, shall we sign the contract now?

213
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:33,580
Uh...

214
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:37,300
Old man,
does the contract cover the cliff top too?

215
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:40,020
Yeah, it's included, I reckon.

216
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:46,660
No matter where you look, there aren't
any decent matsutake around here.

217
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:51,020
Chief, sign quickly.

218
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:56,020
Just write your name
here and that'll be fine.

219
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,180
Well, then.

220
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:05,500
Chief, please sign the contract right now.

221
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:11,000
But I still don't want to
do anything like gambling.

222
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:13,440
That's enough! I said no more!

223
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:17,800
Hey!

224
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:20,640
Ryotsu!

225
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:22,680
Hey! Is this good enough?

226
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,760
You're something else!

227
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:26,620
What do you say, old man!

228
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:28,960
This seals the contract.

229
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,180
I see.

230
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,260
It's not covered in matsutake, but

231
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:52,860
I never imagined the cliff
top was a red pine forest.

232
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,980
Since nobody's ever disturbed it,

233
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:57,280
it's grown up this big, you know.

234
00:14:57,280 --> 00:15:00,160
Hey, this is like striking a gold mine.

235
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,500
We did it, senpai.

236
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:02,455
Ryotsu,

237
00:15:02,505 --> 00:15:05,520
thanks to you, we made a great purchase.

238
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:08,380
Nah, we just hit the jackpot.

239
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:11,540
Please call me Matsutake Hunter Ryotsu.

240
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:16,820
If there was a place like this,
we shouldn't have leased it out.

241
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:21,480
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

242
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:27,240
Matsutake Hunter Ryotsu

243
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:40,500
Thieves have broken
into my matsutake forest!

244
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:43,960
The matsutake forest Ryo-chan found?

245
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:47,820
That spot was even featured in the newspapers and on TV,
you know.

246
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:51,960
Yes, Kameari Park Police Box.

247
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:54,040
Ryo-chan?

248
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:58,620
Have you seen the paper? I couldn't sit still,
so I came over first thing this morning.

249
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:05,300
It's terrible. They took all the
big matsutake and uprooted everything.

250
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:06,460
Ryotsu?

251
00:16:07,020 --> 00:16:10,640
Chief, rest assured.
I'll harvest all of them right now.

252
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:11,680
Wait.

253
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:16,720
I promised Hiromi and the others I'd take
them matsutake hunting on our next day off.

254
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:20,200
If the matsutake aren't properly growing,
Daisuke will...

255
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:22,840
Grandpa's a liar, they'll say.

256
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:24,700
It's fine, Chief.

257
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:28,180
If we wait until the next holiday,
new matsutake will all come up.

258
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:29,640
Is that so?

259
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:33,460
Good. Whatever it takes,
protect the matsutake from the thieves.

260
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:36,260
Then I'll give you as
much matsutake as you want.

261
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:37,520
Really?

262
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,640
As much matsutake as I want?

263
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:41,800
Yes, I'll keep my promise.

264
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:42,360
Understood.

265
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:43,800
Leave it to me.

266
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,700
I bought the food, Senpai.

267
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:48,620
We're really going to protect
the matsutake no matter what!

268
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:53,880
We have to at least do this much.

269
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:55,400
Senpai.

270
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:01,200
The cats got there first.

271
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,220
There you are! Caught you!

272
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:15,380
Looks like they got away.

273
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:16,900
It's too big for just
the two of us to guard.

274
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:19,960
At this rate,
the thieves will do whatever they want.

275
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,040
Ryotsu, boss.

276
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,780
They're pros.

277
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:25,480
Right, let's contact him.

278
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:53,300
Senpai, I've brought the best
members from Nakagawa Security.

279
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:54,320
Alright!

280
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:59,200
General, I, Ryotsu Kankishi,
will be commanding this operation.

281
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,160
Isn't this a bit excessive?

282
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:04,040
This is just right.

283
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:08,540
Listen up! The objective of this
operation is to protect the matsutake.

284
00:18:08,540 --> 00:18:11,760
In other words, we just need to keep
intruders from getting onto the cliff.

285
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:15,900
We'll hold this line and absolutely
establish a matsutake defense zone.

286
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:18,960
All personnel,
give it your all and follow my orders.

287
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:19,980
Let's go!

288
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,300
This is quite a tight defense

289
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:41,020
Rumor has it there's a huge stash
of top-quality matsutake here.

290
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,460
The top of the cliff is
the right spot, right?

291
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,860
That's it, Actroboss!

292
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:07,680
You're not getting away!

293
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:11,800
I'll settle this with
the sword's punishment!

294
00:19:19,940 --> 00:19:22,560
Alright, Third Squad, capture the target!

295
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,140
Roger.

296
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:24,720
That's the tenth one.

297
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:27,400
Looks like we can keep the Chief's matsutake intact,
at least.

298
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,015
Yeah. Of course.

299
00:19:29,065 --> 00:19:31,840
No one could break through this defense net!

300
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:35,520
Unbelievable.

301
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:38,480
Even with security this tight.

302
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,340
Looks like there's a top-notch pro at work.

303
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,840
Damn, persistent thieves.

304
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:46,460
The infrared camera at
C24 caught the culprit.

305
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:48,700
Hand it over.

306
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,940
These thieves look like total klutzes,
don't they?

307
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,200
Yes, Matsutake Defense Squad.

308
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:00,460
Senpai, it's Chief Ohara.

309
00:20:00,460 --> 00:20:01,060
What?

310
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:02,940
It's Ryotsu, is it?

311
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:04,920
How are the matsutake doing?

312
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:06,600
Have they grown?

313
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:08,820
Yes, of course, Chief.

314
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:12,780
Tomorrow, Hiromi and her husband are coming along with Daisuke for the matsutake hunt,
so

315
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:14,700
count on you.

316
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:15,460
Well then,

317
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:18,960
tomorrow.

318
00:20:23,580 --> 00:20:24,920
We're revising the plan.

319
00:20:25,380 --> 00:20:29,080
We can't let a single
more matsutake be stolen.

320
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:30,660
It's an all-out battle.

321
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:55,740
Your every move is plain to see.

322
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:57,520
Do it.

323
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:10,900
You've given us a real run-around,
you bastard.

324
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:12,980
We're going to give you
a proper thank-you for it.

325
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:14,700
Prepare yourself, here we go!

326
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:16,740
Senpai, the defense switch is still -

327
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:18,620
W-what?

328
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:19,960
Aaaaaaah!

329
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:25,980
Eeeeeeeh!

330
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,160
Don't let the suspect get away!

331
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,340
Roger.

332
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:37,520
Wait a minute, are you trying to kill me?

333
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:39,700
Fire! Fire!

334
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:41,860
Baka gara baka gaa!

335
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:45,760
Oops, wrong one.

336
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:47,840
Move out! Cease fire!

337
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,420
It's too late!

338
00:22:04,260 --> 00:22:06,820
Damn, it's turned into a civil war.

339
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:10,040
Can't be helped. Fall back up top!

340
00:22:12,140 --> 00:22:13,120
Thief!

341
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:14,620
Hey! Get back here!

342
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,220
Charge! Charge! Charge!

343
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,720
You stole the matsutake, didn't you!

344
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:21,200
Hey!

345
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:23,180
So you're the thief!

346
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:27,740
The matsutake thief's you, I reckon.

347
00:22:27,740 --> 00:22:28,620
What?

348
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:31,820
I only took back my own matsutake!

349
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:34,140
What nonsense are you spouting!

350
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:35,420
There he is!

351
00:22:38,820 --> 00:22:40,540
Enough already, you lot!

352
00:22:45,860 --> 00:22:48,180
Oh no, this is going to be a disaster.

353
00:23:08,980 --> 00:23:10,210
I'm sure it was, I'm sure,

354
00:23:10,260 --> 00:23:14,100
the matsutake forest I rented
should have been right here.

355
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:17,920
Here it is!

356
00:23:18,290 --> 00:23:18,860
Ryotsu!

357
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:23,360
Good morning, Chief.

358
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:26,300
What on earth is going on here?

359
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:31,040
It's all because we were trying
to protect your matsutake, Chief.

360
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:36,360
So this is your doing!

361
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:41,380
You idiot!

362
00:23:41,380 --> 00:23:42,140
Aaaaaah!

363
00:23:45,420 --> 00:23:50,540
Ugh... you should stay buried right here
and become fertilizer for the matsutake.

364
00:23:50,540 --> 00:23:58,140
At least make up for your sins, farewell. Chief,
that's unreasonable! This is too much for me!

365
00:23:58,140 --> 00:23:59,240
Ugh...

366
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:00,120
That's too much!

367
00:24:04,980 --> 00:24:08,900
Yikes! Maria!
What happened to her biological father?

368
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:11,500
When did she become a real woman?!

369
00:24:11,820 --> 00:24:14,060
Whoa! There's a Maria over here too?

370
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:17,960
W-wait, you guys were ageless people?
I had no idea!

371
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:21,560
Next time: Honda Rakken in a narrow escape!
See you then!

372
00:24:30,460 --> 00:24:37,180
They say I'm a woman who can't fall in love,

373
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:42,960
but I have mountains of things I want to do.

374
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride my motorbike
across the wide desert.

375
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,160
I want to be freer than a bird.

376
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:07,100
A lady's dreams shift as
fast as a kaleidoscope.

377
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:15,080
Sorry, my heart of love, I'm giving in.

378
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:22,220
The dazzle of living out a panoramic future.

379
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:26,502
You understand, right?

380
00:25:26,552 --> 00:25:30,100
Sorry, just wait for me.

